{
  "dom_id": "step-q79",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Solve the equation $3\\cdot {5}^{s}=75.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by dividing both sides by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {5}^{s} & =75 \\\\ \\frac{3\\cdot {5}^{s}}{3} & =\\frac{75}{3} \\\\ {5}^{s} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $25$ as ${5}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{s} & =25 \\\\ {5}^{s} & ={5}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{s} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ s & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $s=2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
